# Template only — no real values here. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# These are the *browser's* half of the app: Supabase Auth, and nothing else.
# The ledger is reached through the .NET API, which is configured separately in
# server/Tracksesh.Api/appsettings*.json.
#
# Hosted Supabase: Project Settings -> API Keys.
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
#
# Local Supabase (`supabase start`) prints both on boot.
#
# Use the *publishable* key (sb_publishable_...), not a secret key.
# Anything VITE_* is inlined into the browser bundle at build time.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Where the API lives. Defaults to /api, which `vite dev` proxies to the API
# process (see vite.config.ts) and which is same-origin in production, because
# the same process serves both. Only set this if you host them apart — and then
# the API needs Cors:AllowedOrigins set to match.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
